Fix over-long meta descriptions to re-enable strict SEO build gate

Task #959 — the SEO validate plugin was reporting ~10,400 prerendered
pages with meta descriptions over the 155-char limit (most flagged at
~195 chars), so both the bundle-size-gate workflow and Vercel had been
silently bypassing the gate.

Root cause
- `esc155(s)` in vite-plugin-prerender.ts did `esc(s.slice(0, 155))`:
  it sliced the *raw* description to 155 chars, then HTML-escaped it.
  Many service labels contain `&` ("Tours & Activities", "Beauty & Hair",
  etc.), and `&` → `&amp;` adds 4 chars per occurrence, easily pushing
  the final HTML attribute past 155 chars (the value the SEO validator
  actually measures via `[^"]*`).

Fix
- Rewrote esc155 to escape *first* then truncate the escaped output to
  155 chars, with a guard that never splits an HTML entity in half
  (backs the cut up to before any unclosed `&…;`).
- esc155 output is now mathematically guaranteed ≤155 chars, so the
  gate's "Description exceeds 155 chars" issue count drops to 0.

Bypass cleanup
- Removed `SEO_GATE_BYPASS: '1'` env from .github/workflows/bundle-
  size-gate.yml (and the long comment justifying it).
- Removed the `process.env.VERCEL === "1"` auto-bypass in
  vite-plugin-seo-validate.ts; only the manual SEO_GATE_BYPASS=1
  emergency switch remains, with a comment explaining its scope.

Verification
- Unit-tested the new esc155 against worst-case inputs (heavy `&`
  density, entity-on-boundary, long pure-ASCII): output stays ≤155 in
  every case and never emits a split entity.
- A full `npm run build` was attempted but OOM'd in this environment
  during chunk rendering for the 12k+ prerendered pages, so end-to-end
  validation will happen on the next CI/Vercel build. The fix is
  provably correct by construction (every meta/og/twitter description
  in vite-plugin-prerender.ts routes through esc155).

Follow-up #964 proposes a fast unit test so this regression is caught
in seconds instead of after a full production build.

